+### Cloned real-league test templates (`backend/test_templates.py`)
+
+Same ALLOWLIST-ONLY gate as `/api/test-users`. Lets an allowlisted operator snapshot their OWN real league(s) into an isolated namespace so `qa_*` spawns can clone a realistic player pool + opponents instead of the 10-player demo fixture. **Isolation namespace:** every snapshot is stored under a `qatest_<realleagueid>_<4hex>` league id in the same `leagues` + `league_members` tables real leagues use (safe because those tables are only ever read by PK/league_id); opponent member ids are rewritten to `qaopp_<n>` so nothing under a `qatest_` league carries a real routable Sleeper id. **Read-only on real data:** capture only INSERTs new `qatest_` rows — it never mutates the operator's real `leagues`/`league_members`/`member_rankings`. **Analytics exclusion:** `qa_*`, `qatest_*`, and `qaopp_*` ids are stripped from cohort reports at `analytics_queries.device_exclusion` (and the inline `demo_` predicates were extended to also drop `qa_`).
